{"uid":"4c2b0999a17cb021","name":"test_run_detail_marks_a_dead_dependencys_subtree_blocked","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub#test_run_detail_marks_a_dead_dependencys_subtree_blocked","historyId":"2877c37c83333029ca4648e82f8b4418","time":{"start":1791958117411,"stop":1791958133902,"duration":16491},"description":"A dependency that reaches `failed`/`skipped` dooms its dependents\n    WITHOUT the harness ever changing their own `status` -- and the hub\n    shows it, not just `ralphctl tasks`, per the PRD's own wording (\"Dead\n    subtrees are visible in `ralphctl tasks` and the hub\").\n\n    Task 004 is dead outright; 005 depends on it directly (blocked); 006\n    depends on 005, which is itself only blocked, not dead -- proving the\n    derivation is transitive, not one hop. Task 007 depends on 001\n    (completed, a SATISFIED dependency) and is NOT blocked.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>A dependency that reaches <code>failed</code>/<code>skipped</code> dooms its dependents<br />\nWITHOUT the harness ever changing their own <code>status</code> -- and the hub<br />\nshows it, not just <code>ralphctl tasks</code>, per the PRD's own wording (&quot;Dead<br />\nsubtrees are visible in <code>ralphctl tasks</code> and the hub&quot;).</p>\n<pre><code>Task 004 is dead outright; 005 depends on it directly (blocked); 006\ndepends on 005, which is itself only blocked, not dead -- proving the\nderivation is transitive, not one hop. Task 007 depends on 001\n(completed, a SATISFIED dependency) and is NOT blocked.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791957833013,"stop":1791957833014,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791